"## Summary\n\nMembers follow-up 22: the D-098 archive of run `5715939e`, the evidence F21-AT08 and F21-D146 lacked, the G2 archive alias, and one assembled run on agent-core 50, judged by unchanged predicates.\n- **Session:** launched 02:42 EST on 2026-11-04 on #461's roadmap row, and delivered at 04:17.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 8 commits and 364 owned files, +1,245,206/−145,840. Almost all of it is records: the D-098 archive and the new run's records. The largest file is 12.5 MB, and the total is 205.7 MB.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (after #463) with secops 18 and this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-members.mk at-members-lint`;\n    - `go test ./tests/e2e/at/members/...`, with and without `-tags e2e`;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`, including `TestCommittedEvidenceHygiene`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`;\n    - `python3 -B tests/e2e/at/members/followup22_records.py`, which rebuilt every follow-up 22 index from the measured originals byte for byte.\n- **Scope:** one assembled run in the lane's own namespace, after one allowed own-harness pre-check rerun, and no reservation. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n  - **Attempt 1** waited 21 minutes for admission, then stopped before `go test` and before any acceptance check. The lane's own `admission.py` met a host command line with an unmatched quote and raised `ValueError: No closing quotation`.\n    - The matching line was not retained. Orchestrator commands are a plausible source: their note text often has an apostrophe and names those targets.\n    - Fixed in `8a6dcf34`, with four offline tests.\n  - **The retry** needed no admission wait.\n  - **Its one foreign window,** 09:08:22–09:08:52Z, came after the acceptance command ended at 09:08:08.8Z, during teardown. It is the merge queue's gates for updater 25 (pid 517476, `bash`), which started at 09:08:15Z. The lane recorded it as confounded under D-133; it intersects no measured case.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-098 first** (`1767a389`): run `5715939e`'s 98 root records are archived byte-identically under `history/follow-up-21/`, with SHA-256 pins. Every earlier archive is untouched.\n  - **Links:** 633 relative links resolve, including follow-up 18 run 2's three frozen G2 links, through the new alias (`049dc614`).\n- **The run:** `3eb3960d` on harness `8a6dcf34`, baseline `55f2765d`, which is `main` after agent-core 50 (#461). **3 pass, 7 blocked, 0 fail; 702 passed, 8 blocked and 0 failed subchecks.** Exit 2 because of the blocked rows.\n  - AT02, AT03 and AT08 pass. AT01, AT04, AT05, AT09, AT20, AT21 and AT22 are blocked.\n  - **Against run `5715939e`:**\n    - AT08 goes from blocked to pass, and gains one native-capture check;\n    - AT01's first transfer goes from counted to uncounted, so its four conditional continuation checks were not reached.\n    - That is 705 − 4 + 1 = 702. No predicate was removed. Every earlier run keeps its recorded outcome.\n- **The lane's first request, the baseline: no later-`main` run is needed.**\n  - The run measured `55f2765d`. Only #462 merged before the retry's preflight, and it changed only `docs/` and `tests/netlab/`. No product file and no members path changed.\n  - So the run measured the same product and members code as `main` when the retry started. #463 merged after delivery.\n- **AT02, under D-157:**\n  - **one early renewal:** its one closed recovery has a renewal request 67.8 ms after closed-recovery Apply 586, then a one-member lease, then verified serving Apply 592. There is exactly one request, and no baseline write between them;\n  - **the de